{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/522165-the-lands-of-demons-france-and-italy","id":522165,"title":"The Lands of Demons- France and Italy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-20T12:06:34-07:00","id":522165,"title":"The Lands of Demons- France and Italy","content":"while working on my &quot;mapping the hunter orgs around the globe&quot; list, I've noticed something that has avoided me earlier- while the Lucifuge is based in Italy, the leadership of their dark counterpart, the Lenfant Diaboliqu, is found in France. Also, from what we have in the Dark Eras, the Silent Imperative (which was founded by with the help of Lady Lucifuge and may have helped her escape once or twice) has been showed up first in France. That made me think- what if the Lenfant Diabolique's creation is connected to the witch hunts? What if the Three Blind Men are former Lucifuge who have been blinded by the hunts of the Inquisition, survived and have decided to embrace their &quot;true self&quot;- that is, if they are hunted like demons, why should't they act like ones? What if the original Silent Imperative wasn't much disbanded as it was destroyed by the Three? What if the Lady hasn't escaped the Church as she escaped her former agents? And what is going on today between France and Italy in the shadows of the world? I mean, considering the range of the two groups and the fact that they fight over the same resource (meaning, Children of the 7th Generation), shouldn't it mean that there is at least a &quot;cold war&quot; between the two? Or maybe they have some non aggression pact in which they divide each new Child among themselves- which means how is it that those members who are not found by the Lucifuge always show up in the hands of the Lefnant?<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T16:27:13-07:00","id":522632,"title":"","content":"Sounds reasonable. The Lady of Milan is old enough she's probably been caught in some tough situations, it's possible she made a few deals to escape them with hide intact.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the Faustians of the Mercy Seat, a faction of Belial's Brood, have their 'largest and oldest' stronghold in the site of the faction's Renaissance, the city of Genoa, Italy. They're aiming for the Vatican, of course, but have always been big in the northern city states of Italy.<br /> <br /> Italy probably gets mentioned a lot with demons and demon accessories due to it being central to the Church.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-20-2015, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T17:06:59-07:00","id":522674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/522165-the-lands-of-demons-france-and-italy#post522165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while working on my &quot;mapping the hunter orgs around the globe&quot; list, I've noticed something that has avoided me earlier- while the Lucifuge is based in Italy, the leadership of their dark counterpart, the Lenfant Diaboliqu, is found in France. Also, from what we have in the Dark Eras, the Silent Imperative (which was founded by with the help of Lady Lucifuge and may have helped her escape once or twice) has been showed up first in France. That made me think- what if the Lenfant Diabolique's creation is connected to the witch hunts? What if the Three Blind Men are former Lucifuge who have been blinded by the hunts of the Inquisition, survived and have decided to embrace their &quot;true self&quot;- that is, if they are hunted like demons, why should't they act like ones? What if the original Silent Imperative wasn't much disbanded as it was destroyed by the Three? What if the Lady hasn't escaped the Church as she escaped her former agents? And what is going on today between France and Italy in the shadows of the world? I mean, considering the range of the two groups and the fact that they fight over the same resource (meaning, Children of the 7th Generation), shouldn't it mean that there is at least a &quot;cold war&quot; between the two? Or maybe they have some non aggression pact in which they divide each new Child among themselves- which means how is it that those members who are not found by the Lucifuge always show up in the hands of the Lefnant?<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an upcoming game in Paris. It's Changeling based, so hunters aren't going to come in gameplay(at all, for once), but this is a nifty enough idea I'm incorporating it into the background of the setting, helping to frame the story.<br /> <br /> I know I'm going to have more games in Paris, so it will come more into prevalence later one, because I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}